  "description": "T1 - Magnolia - Crown Reduction by 2.0 to 3.0 metres pruning back to previous pruning points or suitable, Crown Lift up to 2.5 metres from ground level, Crown Thin by a maximum of 15%. \r\rT2 -Sycamore -  Crown lift up to 2.5m from ground level, Remove the lowest secondary limbs overhanging the garden area by cutting back cleanly to the branch collar at the primary trunk axis. Avoid wounds exceeding 100mm in diameter to preserve structural integrity and prevent epicormic re-growth.  \r\rT3 - Amelanchier  -  Crown Reduction 0.3 to 0.5 metres, Crown Thin by a maximum of 10%. \r\rT4 - Leylandii -  Lateral Pruning (Boundary Clearance): Prune back sagging, overhanging foliage on the rear boundary fence line by shortening lateral branches by 1.0 to 1.5 metres,Trim Conifer branch growth away from the Betula pendul\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r",
